    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥητορ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be a public speaker, practise oratory</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				8.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				502d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.Al.</u>
				1444a33
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μετὰ γαστέρα
			-εύοντες</span> afterdinner <i>speakers</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.156
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. καὶ πολιτεύεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					3.175
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολιτεύεσθαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Nausiph.
				2
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, of the speech, <i>to be spoken</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς μὲν [λόγους] ῥητορεύεσθαι, τοὺς
					δὲ γεγράφθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					5.25
				</span></i>
			:—later in 
				Act.
			 c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἐπεσταλμένην
				πρεσβείαν ἐρρητόρευε</span>
			<i>was setting forth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Laps.</u>
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
